          ],
          "text ": "Who We Are:The Data Sherpas are a team of highly skilled and motivated engineers that help our clients at every phase of their cloud journey. If it touches the cloud, involves data, or lives as an application, we have either worked on it or have the skills and expertise to accomplish it. &#92;nWhat We Are Looking For:We seek an experienced and talented individual to build and maintain the data infrastructure that powers our advertising platform. It is the perfect role for an individual who wants to work on unique and challenging problems that will have a meaningful impact on the Ad Tech industry. This is a contact position working with our Data and Backend Teams. This contract will be 6-12 months.&#92;nWhat You &#39;ll Do:Design and maintain the data infrastructure for the Ad Tech platform.Develop data processing pipelines.Understand and address customers &#39;data needs.Collaborate with teams to identify and prioritize data requirements.Implement monitoring and alerting mechanisms for the data infrastructure.Stay abreast of the latest data engineering tools and technologies.Create and update technical documentation.Uphold excellence in software and data engineering practices.Ensure compliance with data governance requirements.&#92;nWhat You Have:Proficiency in Java and Scala, with the ability to incorporate new technologies within existing codebases.Extensive experience with Apache Spark, including optimizing Spark clusters for performance and scalability.Comprehensive knowledge of the Ad Tech ecosystem, including working with large-scale audience data and ad platforms.Advanced analytical skills to interpret complex data, identify trends, and derive insights.Experience in data profiling and analyzing both structured and unstructured data.Proven track record in designing and implementing data models for data-driven marketing campaigns.Experience creating audience segments for targeted advertising and integrating with third-party Ad Tech data sources.Familiarity with data governance requirements, particularly handling anonymized or aggregate data.&#92;nWe cannot work with third-party agencies at this time. Resumes submitted via unapproved agencies will be automatically rejected.",
          "$type ": "com.linkedin.pemberly.text.AttributedText "
        },
